<p>The process of painting a sunflower sunset. Painting with the light workshop with Amanda sage. 
<!-- excerpt end --></p>

<h2 id="the-start">The start</h2>

<p>This was the second time I was attending a workshop with Amanda Sage, an amazing artist I have met through my partner. The one thing I learnt from the first workshop was to not overthink it and to trust the process. I was then decided to not overthink drawing this flower. My favorite color (right now, and for the past 10 years or so) is yellow, so I picked a yellow flower as a reference. I started with a rough sketch of the flower, trying not to obsess over getting it perfectly. This was not only a workshop to practice painting to me, it also is a workshop to practice being kind and forgiving to myself. I then started with the light and the dark process, which is the core of this technique; alternating light and dark layers until…it works. Then came in the colors.</p>

